{
  "item": "Object01",
  "mu_name": "Object01",
  "mu_name_from": "Devias's object slot 0, which is the model index: every world but Lorencia runs its objects in one straight sequence, so type N is Object{N+1}.bmd and there is no friendlier name in the client than the number.",
  "world": "devias",
  "object_type": 0,
  "placements": 451,
  "profile": "world",
  "sheets": {
    "stree_jpg": "dv_stree_jpg.png",
    "stree_tga": "dv_stree_tga.png"
  },
  "sheet_from": "Data/Object3/stree.OZJ and stree.OZT, from MuMain, decoded under a dv_ prefix. The prefix is load-bearing as nr_ is for Noria: assets/textures is one flat pool, and 39 of Object3's sheet names are already in it. The two share a stem, so the mesh groups are stree_jpg and stree_tga, as PantElf02's are.",
  "sheet_materials": {
    "stree_jpg": "bark",
    "stree_tga": "foliage"
  },
  "material_note": "stree_jpg: grey furrowed bark, the trunk.\nstree_tga: a fir's crown under snow - white drifts on dark green needles, the edge cut out. Foliage rather than snow, because it is thin cards lit through: the snow is painted on the needles.",
  "cutout": [
    "stree_tga"
  ],
  "cutout_from": "stree.OZT carries a real alpha channel, cutting away 55%, as decode_texture reports it.",
  "why_this_one": "Devias's commonest object, 451 of 2235: the snowy fir the whole map is planted with. First on the worklist.",
  "animation_note": "Rigged: 12 bones, one action of 30 keys, a sway. MuMain's WD_2DEVIAS arm gives type 0 nothing else -- no light, no blend mesh, no emitter (ZzzObject.cpp CreateObject :4668-4720, RenderObjectVisual :2819-2836, MoveObject :3900-3964) -- so it plays at CreateObject's 0.16.",
